From de1e845929c2aad0ed9720db9e1149e4910dbbbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olivier Moysan <olivier.moysan@foss.st.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 11:00:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: connector: synchronize hdmi state on hpd

The bridge connector HPD callback only updates the connector status and
emits a hotplug event. Unlike the detect path, it does not update the HDMI
state, leaving the EDID, ELD and audio plug state stale after an HPD event.
Call the HDMI hotplug helper for connectors backed by an HDMI bridge.

Change-Id: I32df6f4e76fcba343cd8199c676a7b3d5af574e8
Assisted-by: GitHub-Copilot:GPT:5.6-Sol
Signed-off-by: Olivier Moysan <olivier.moysan@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/613145
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Yannick FERTRE <yannick.fertre@foss.st.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_bridge_connector.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_bridge_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_bridge_connector.c
@@ -156,6 +156,10 @@ static void drm_bridge_connector_handle_
 	connector->status = status;
 	mutex_unlock(&dev->mode_config.mutex);
 
+	/* Keep HDMI EDID/ELD and audio plug state synchronized with HPD. */
+	if (drm_bridge_connector->bridge_hdmi)
+		drm_atomic_helper_connector_hdmi_hotplug(connector, status);
+
 	drm_bridge_connector_hpd_notify(connector, status);
 
 	drm_kms_helper_connector_hotplug_event(connector);
